concepts.content:
In summary, we get that The DFT of the box function is the discrete sinc function: 
$$\text{box}_{L} \left[n \right]\xrightarrow{\mathscr{F}} 
\frac{\sin \pi u (2L+1)/N}{\sin \pi u/N}
$$ 

We will denote the DFT of the box function, $\text{box}_{L} \left[n \right]$, capitalizing the first letter, $\text{Box}_{L} \left[u \right]$. This function has its maximum value at $u=0$. The DFT, $\text{Box}_{L} \left[u \right]$, is a symmetric real function. The following plot (@fig-boxfilterdft) shows the DFT of the box with $L=5$, and $N=32$. One period of the DFT is contained in the interval $\left[ -16, 15 \right]$ and the rest is a periodic extension.

